# MaxMailServer — Gmail Bridge Configuration
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your details.
# NEVER commit .env to git.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your Gmail address
GMAIL_USER=yourmail@gmail.com

# Gmail App Password (NOT your regular Gmail password)
# How to generate one:
#   1. Go to https://myaccount.google.com/security
#   2. Enable 2-Step Verification (required)
#   3. Search for "App Passwords"
#   4. Create a new App Password → choose "Mail" + "Windows Computer"
#   5. Copy the 16-character code (spaces are OK) and paste it below
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Device Pairing (Security)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MaxMail uses device pairing to ensure only your BlackBerry can
# access this server. No secrets are stored in source code.
#
# To pair a new device:
#   1. Start the server in pairing mode:
#      PAIR_MODE=true node server.js
#   2. A 6-digit PIN will appear in the console
#   3. Open MaxMail on your BlackBerry → Settings → enter the PIN → Pair
#   4. The PIN expires after 5 minutes or first use
#   5. Restart the server normally: node server.js
#
# Paired devices are stored in paired_devices.json (auto-created).
# To unpair all devices, delete paired_devices.json and restart.
